.TH BOOTSTASHD 8 "September 2026" "bootstash" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bootstashd \- convenience cubby for bootstrap files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstashd
[\fB\-V\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fB\-defaults\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstashd
is the bootstash daemon. After Google OpenID Connect and a one-time PAM
link to an existing Unix account, it serves a shared tree (read) and the
linked user’s tree (read/write) over HTTP or HTTPS.
.PP
HTTP
.B DELETE
removes a file or empty directory in a writable tree (not rename).
.PP
It is a convenience store, not a high-assurance secrets engine. Isolation
is a path jail plus POSIX permissions; the process runs as one service
user
.BR bootstash .
.PP
The daemon refuses to start until
.B PUBLIC_ORIGIN
is set or can be derived from
.B hostname \-f
and the first TCP
.B BIND
port, and
.B OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
is set (usually the Google client JSON in
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version from
.B git describe
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-check\-config
Parse dist defaults, operator config, secrets file, BIND specs, and
TLS files (if set). Print a short summary and exit. Does not listen.
.TP
.BI \-defaults " path"
Dist defaults file. Default:
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist .
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Operator config. Default:
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.TP
.BI \-secrets " path"
OIDC client secrets. Default:
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read dist defaults, operator config, and the secrets file
(keep the last good config on parse failure),
reload TLS certificate and key from disk (keep the previous cert on
failure), and re-sync CIDR/interface listeners without dropping unrelated
listeners. systemd
.B reload
sends this.
.TP
.B SIGTERM / SIGINT
Graceful shutdown. Under systemd the process sends
.B STOPPING=1
then closes listeners.
.PP
The packaged unit is
.B Type=notify
.RB ( READY=1
after config is loaded, including while waiting for a missing interface).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist
Dist defaults (not a conffile).
.TP
.I /etc/default/bootstash
Operator config; commented keys matching
.I default-dist
on install. See
.BR bootstash (5).
.TP
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
Google OIDC client id/secret. Written by
.B bootstash provision-google .
Not a conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bootstash
Default data volume:
.IR shared/ ,
.IR users/<pam_user>/
.RB ( 2770
.IR alice:bootstash ),
.IR state/
.RB ( 0700 ,
not served).
Removing the package does not delete
.I shared/
or
.IR users/ ;
those are operator files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstash (8),
.BR bootstash (5),
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/QUICKSTART.md
